post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

  Filthy Net Deck is installed.

  Hyprland users — add one line to your config. The overlay works without
  it; with it, layer animations stay off for FND's surfaces.

      dofile("/usr/share/filthy-net-deck/hypr/filthy-net-deck.lua")

  Put that line in ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua (or any file it loads),
  run: hyprctl reload — then start (or restart) Arena.

  Leave Arena on Full Screen in its own Graphics menu, and keep your bar
  however you like it. Earlier builds asked you to hide the bar and let
  Hyprland refuse Arena's fullscreen; that turned out not to be what made
  the overlay clickable, and neither is needed any more.

  Match tracking needs Arena's detailed logs:
      Options -> Account -> Detailed Logs (Plugin Support)
  then restart Arena.

  Updates never come from inside the app. Until filthy-net-deck-bin is on
  the AUR (Arch has new-account registration paused), rebuild it from the
  current release — the two lines are at:

      https://filthy-net-deck.com/#download

  Omarchy's crash watcher may pop a "Process crashed: WebKitWebProcess"
  banner when you quit FND. That is WebKitGTK's render process going down
  with its parent on an NVIDIA/Mesa box, not the app losing anything —
  matches are written to disk before shutdown starts.

MSG
}

# Printed on every upgrade, including a reinstall of the same version.
#
# Step 1 is the one people miss. FND runs a single instance: launching it
# again while an old copy is up only brings that old window to the front
# (tauri-plugin-single-instance → show_main_window), so without an explicit
# quit the upgrade silently does nothing until the next reboot. That is how
# 3.9.0 was first "installed" on the maintainer's own machine and still
# reported 3.8.2.
post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'MSG'

  Filthy Net Deck upgraded. To finish:

    1. Quit Filthy Net Deck from its tray icon, then open it again.
       Only one copy ever runs, so opening it while the old one is still
       up just brings the old version back to the front.
    2. hyprctl reload       picks up the updated Hyprland rules
    3. Restart Arena        Proton pointer-grab keys and Hyprland rules
       apply when Arena's window opens. Skip this and the badge can
       look fine but ignore clicks until the next Arena launch.

  Never added the Hyprland line? It keeps the HUD from flickering when it
  re-stacks itself above a notification or a panel:

      dofile("/usr/share/filthy-net-deck/hypr/filthy-net-deck.lua")

MSG
}
